 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Ladder step (line 152): `f i = f (i+1) + t (i+1)`; only `f N = 0` and `t N = 0` are needed to close, both from `genWeightSpace M (\u03c7 + N \u2022 \u03b1) = \u22a5`. Mathlib states the analogous chain results with single-point endpoint vanishing, not eventual vanishing: `Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/Weights/Chain.lean:141` `(hq : genWeightSpace M (q \u2022 \u03b1 + \u03c7) = \u22a5)` and `:178-179` `trace_toEnd_genWeightSpaceChain_eq_zero (hp ...) (hq ...)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/Trace.lean",
   "fix": "Weaken to `hN : genWeightSpace M (\u03c7 + N \u2022 \u03b1) = \u22a5` and restructure the induction as `\u2200 d i, i + d = N \u2192 trace ... = \u2211 j \u2208 Finset.Ico (i+1) N, ...` (base `i = N`, step by `Finset.sum_eq_sum_Ico_succ_bot` with the `i + 1 = N` case handled by `finrank \u22a5 = 0`). `trace_raiseLowerEnd_eq_sum_weightString` still applies it with the `N` from `exists_genWeightSpace_add_nsmul_eq_bot_of_le`, just instantiated at that one `j`.",
   "issue": "`hN : \u2200 j, N \u2264 j \u2192 genWeightSpace M (\u03c7 + j \u2022 \u03b1) = \u22a5` is stronger than the statement needs: the RHS only mentions `j < N`, and the ladder terminates as soon as the single space `M_{\u03c7 + N\u2022\u03b1}` is `\u22a5` (then `raiseLowerEnd` at rung `N` is `0` by `raiseLowerEnd_eq_zero` and the `j = N` term vanishes since `finrank \u22a5 = 0`). The tail beyond `N` never enters the telescope.",
   "line": 169
  }
 ],
